    {
      "element_kind": "section",
      "id": "imported_section_001",
      "role": "model",
      "objective_ids": [
        "obj_negative_fronting"
      ],
      "title": "Negative and Restrictive Openings",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Negative and restrictive expressions can also be fronted for emphasis or a formal written rhythm. A restrictive expression narrows the statement, as with "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "sjelden",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " or "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "knapt",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ". If that expression is first in a main clause, the finite verb still comes second."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "After fronted negative or restrictive expressions in a main clause, use inversion: fronted expression plus finite verb plus subject."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Aldri har jeg sett en så rask løsning."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Never have I seen such a quick solution."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Sjelden får vi så tydelige svar."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Rarely do we get such clear answers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Ingen av forslagene hadde gruppen godkjent."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The group had approved none of the proposals."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Heller ikke i år får vi ekstra støtte."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "This year, too, we are not getting extra support."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Knapt hadde møtet begynt før telefonen ringte."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The meeting had hardly begun before the phone rang."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "level": "warning",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Do not copy English word order after fronted negatives. Norwegian does not say "
                },
                {
                  "kind": "foreign_term",
                  "value": "Aldri jeg har sett det",
                  "lang": "no"
                },
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": " in a main clause. Say "
                },
                {
                  "kind": "foreign_term",
                  "value": "Aldri har jeg sett det",
                  "lang": "no"
                },
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "element_kind": "section",
      "id": "imported_section_002",
      "role": "contrast",
      "objective_ids": [
        "obj_subordinate_boundary"
      ],
      "title": "Main Clauses Versus Subordinate Clauses",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "A subordinate clause is a clause introduced by a word such as "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "fordi",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "at",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "hvis",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", or "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "når",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ". In subordinate clauses, negative and sentence adverbs normally stand before the finite verb: subject plus adverb plus verb."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Use main-clause inversion only in main clauses. Inside subordinate clauses, keep subject plus adverb plus finite verb."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Jeg kommer i morgen hvis møtet ikke varer for lenge."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "I am coming tomorrow if the meeting does not last too long."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Hun sa at hun aldri hadde sett rapporten."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "She said that she had never seen the report."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Vi ble overrasket fordi de sjelden klager."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "We were surprised because they rarely complain."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "level": "tip",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "A quick test helps: if the first word is a subordinator such as "
                },
                {
                  "kind": "foreign_term",
                  "value": "fordi",
                  "lang": "no"
                },
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": " or "
                },
                {
                  "kind": "foreign_term",
                  "value": "at",
                  "lang": "no"
                },
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": ", do not use main-clause inversion inside that clause."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "element_kind": "section",
      "id": "imported_section_003",
      "role": "recap",
      "objective_ids": [
        "obj_v2_fronting",
        "obj_negative_fronting",
        "obj_subordinate_boundary"
      ],
      "title": "The Working Pattern",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The key choice is not whether the first phrase is negative, temporal, or an object. The key choice is whether you are in a main clause or a subordinate clause."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Main clause with a fronted non-subject phrase: phrase plus finite verb plus subject."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Main clause with a fronted negative or restrictive phrase: phrase plus finite verb plus subject."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Subordinate clause: subordinator plus subject plus adverb plus finite verb."
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "I går kom de sent, fordi toget ikke gikk."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Yesterday they arrived late because the train did not run."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
